+# Automation design & responsibilities
+
+This document explains the automation pieces added in this patch, their intent, owners, and what must be filled before production.
+
+1) Vault PKI (ops/infra/terraform)
+ - Purpose: issue short-lived client certs for FL attestation and mTLS.
+ - Owner: Security/SRE. Fill: vault_addr, vault_token, backend config and secure Terraform state.
+
+2) Cosign KMS (Terraform placeholder)
+ - Purpose: create a KMS key to store cosign private key or to be used via KMS-based signing flows.
+ - Owner: Security. Fill: provider-specific KMS resources and IAM controls.
+
+3) Secure aggregation adapter and CI
+ - Purpose: ensure a vetted secure-aggregation library is present and smoke-tested in CI.
+ - Owner: ML/Security. Action: install secagg/crypten in builder images, run flux tests, request crypto review.
+
+4) DeepSpeed autotune pipeline
+ - Purpose: run staged NCCL/ZeRO tuning, collect logs and produce recommended env vars/configs.
+ - Owner: ML Infra. Action: run on representative hardware, store results to S3 and update deepspeed config templates.
+
+5) Webhook & cert-manager automation
+ - Purpose: deploy cert-manager, create certificates for webhooks, patch caBundle to ValidatingWebhookConfiguration.
+ - Owner: Platform/SRE. Action: ensure cluster allows cert-manager and set proper RBAC.
+
+6) Enterprise Gate & scheduled run
+ - Purpose: weekly auto-run of the canonical acceptance pipeline and production evidence bundle creation.
+ - Owner: Platform/Compliance. Action: set GitHub secrets and verify runner permissions before enabling schedule.
+
+Security & operational cautions
+- Do not run Terraform scripts against production Vault without Change Control and backups.
+- Do not set ALLOW_INSECURE_SECAGG=1 in production. It's only for dev smoke tests.
+- Protect COSIGN_KMS_URI and VAULT tokens in CI secrets and use GitHub OIDC where possible.
+
